{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And Jethro took… a burnt-offering, etc.</b> Now Jethro was clever to slaughter many peace-offerings, and this served as a sign that he was inviting the great men of Israel to his table. Therefore Scripture did not say, ״And he called Aaron and the elders of Israel to eat,״ etc., but rather <b>and Aaron came</b>, etc. — meaning, they came of their own accord, for his actions made the invitation self-evident, so that the consecrated portions would not become leftover meat (notar). They honored him and came of their own accord — Aaron and the elders — and did not trouble him to invite them to the feast."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:29:32.703447361Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}